.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt SLEEP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sleep
.Nd suspend execution for an interval
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar seconds
.Nm
.Fl -selftest
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
suspends the calling process for
.Ar seconds
whole seconds with
.Xr nanosleep 2 .
The value must be a decimal integer that converts to nanoseconds without
overflow.
.Pp
.Fl -selftest
sleeps for one millisecond and prints
.Dq sleep: selftest ok .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error or an overflowing value exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nanosleep 2
.Sh STANDARDS
The operand is a whole number of seconds in this version; fractional seconds
are not accepted.
